n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t 3\\sqrt{3} -3\\sqrt{3} + 3\\sqrt[3]{x^2} - x^2\\sqrt {x} &= \\\\[5pt]\n           (3 -3)\\sqrt{3} + 3\\sqrt[3]{x^2} - x^2\\sqrt {x} &= \\\\[5pt]\n0\\cdot \\sqrt{3} + 3\\sqrt[3]{x^2} - x^2\\sqrt {x} &= \\\\[5pt]\n \t\t 3\\sqrt[3]{x^2} - x^2\\sqrt {x} &\n\t}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":3756,"name":"Adding and Subtracting Radical Expressions"},"example":{"id":1374,"title":"Simplifying Sums of Radicals Using the Product Rule"},"group":{"id":108907,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14246049,"answer":{"id":62283702,"cread":"2026-10-15T16:16:47.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12659},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62283753,"created":"2026-10-15T16:17:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10584,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 4:17 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":29319,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":9723,"text":"<p>Simplify $3\\sqrt[3]{y} - 4\\sqrt{y} - 7\\sqrt[3]{y} + 2\\sqrt{y}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-2\\sqrt{y} -4\\sqrt[3]{y}$","choice2":"$4\\sqrt{y} -2\\sqrt[3]{y}$","choice3":"$-\\sqrt{y} - 5\\sqrt[3]{y}$","choice4":"$-6\\sqrt{y}$","choice5":"$2\\sqrt{y} - 4\\sqrt[3]{y}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ terms together, and the two $\\sqrt{y}$ terms together:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n3\\sqrt[3]{y} - 4\\sqrt{y} - 7\\sqrt[3]{y} + 2\\sqrt{y} &= \\\\[5pt]\n(- 4+2)\\sqrt{y}+ (3 - 7)\\sqrt[3]{y} &= \\\\[5pt]\n-2\\sqrt{y} -4\\sqrt[3]{y}\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Notice that we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ and $\\sqrt{y}$ terms.</p>\n","topic":{"id":3756,"name":"Adding and Subtracting Radical Expressions"},"example":{"id":9723,"title":"Simplifying Sums of Radicals with Cube Roots"},"group":{"id":108909,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14246049,"answer":{"id":62283753,"cread":"2026-10-15T16:17:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10584},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62283825,"created":"2026-10-15T16:17:18.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11637,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 4:17 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":29322,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":1374,"text":"<p>Simplify $2x\\sqrt{54} + 2x\\sqrt{x} -5x\\sqrt{6}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$x\\sqrt{6} + 2x\\sqrt{x}$","choice2":"$x\\sqrt 6 -x\\sqrt{x}$","choice3":"$x$","choice4":"$\\sqrt 6 +\\sqrt{x}$","choice5":"$x\\sqrt 6$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\\[\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t2x\\sqrt{54} + 2x\\sqrt{x} -5x\\sqrt{6} &= \\\\[5pt]\n \t\t  2x\\sqrt{9 \\cdot 6} + 2x\\sqrt{x}  -5x\\sqrt{6}&= \\\\[5pt]\n2x\\sqrt{9} \\cdot \\sqrt{6} + 2x\\sqrt{x}  -5x\\sqrt{6}&= \\\\[5pt]\n2x\\cdot 3 \\cdot \\sqrt{6}  + 2x\\sqrt{x} -5x\\sqrt{6}&= \\\\[5pt]\n6x\\sqrt{6} + 2x\\sqrt{x} -5x\\sqrt{6}&\n\t}\n\\]\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\\[\n\t\\eqalign{\n         6x\\sqrt{6} + 2x\\sqrt{x} -5x\\sqrt{6}&= \\\\[5pt]\n        (6x -5x)\\sqrt{6} + 2x\\sqrt{x}&= \\\\[5pt]\n \t x\\sqrt{6} + 2x\\sqrt{x}\n\t}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":3756,"name":"Adding and Subtracting Radical Expressions"},"example":{"id":1374,"title":"Simplifying Sums of Radicals Using the Product Rule"},"group":{"id":108907,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14246049,"answer":{"id":62283825,"cread":"2026-10-15T16:17:18.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11637},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficul